{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1427345-defense-enchancement","id":1427345,"title":"Defense enchancement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-05T04:10:41-08:00","id":1427345,"title":"Defense enchancement","content":"Hello guys!<br /> <br /> A player on my game asked me yestarday, if he could create a birthright with enchancement on his defense. I didnt see anything on game so far to improve defense like that, im kinda afraid to broke the game. So what you guys think that birthright is not a big deal? Or defense is not suppose to get enchancement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T04:50:05-08:00","id":1427346,"title":"","content":"Yup you can have an enhancement on any standard rolls, so defende would definitely work.<br /> <br /> In addition you could also justify making a feat of scale and gaining scale with your defense roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T06:24:15-08:00","id":1427354,"title":"","content":"Soft Armor is something you can gain through a Birthright and is basically an Enhancement to Defence since it increases the amount of successes you need to Hurt someone. So you could tell your player that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T06:31:11-08:00","id":1427355,"title":"","content":"That would depend on what the relic is tho.<br /> If its an armor or piece of clothing then extra soft armor would be a good idea.<br /> But if its a sword or something similar then soft armor could be a weird fot (tho not impossible either)<br /> <br /> Hm rereading the OP post, you just say birthright.<br /> Do you mean relic or are yoy also asking if a Guide could give enhancement on the defense roll?<br /> (The answer would be i think itd be fine for a guide stunt to give a enhancement bonus for the next x defense rolls)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T07:32:35-08:00","id":1427365,"title":"","content":"Trinity have the Shield weapon tag that add 1 enhancement to defense rolls, it may be used for shields or weapons designed to defense, like main gauche. So, it opens precedence to using a weapon as defensive tool. Also, Shields are called weapons in many references, defensive weapons, but weapons.<br /> <br /> But you can consider the enhancement granted by relics to apply to defense rolls (in this case not applying to other uses). A generic enhancement would apply to all defense rolls, and a specific enhancement only to some attacks (ranged or close combat, for example).<br /> <br /> The motif can be like the Cloths of Saint Seya, giving speed to the knight, or as a divine force field around them, it\u2019s up to the fluffy desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:30:03-08:00","id":1427390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1427345-defense-enchancement?p=1427355#post1427355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would depend on what the relic is tho.<br /> If its an armor or piece of clothing then extra soft armor would be a good idea.<br /> But if its a sword or something similar then soft armor could be a weird fot (tho not impossible either)<br /> <br /> Hm rereading the OP post, you just say birthright.<br /> Do you mean relic or are yoy also asking if a Guide could give enhancement on the defense roll?<br /> (The answer would be i think itd be fine for a guide stunt to give a enhancement bonus for the next x defense rolls)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he asked me about a relic like a armor to help him on defende by enchancement.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys, i was only sorrires to break the sistem somehow, thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}